+### 9. Carry a shared claim field once per scope
+
+The human page carries every claim's complete epistemic tuple, evaluation
+identity and non-authority attributes on the claim's own element. On the
+whole declared Butlers project that repetition is most of the per-item cost:
+after the 2026-09-13 lane A trim the page still sits above the ruled 1.4 MB
+working target under the 2 MiB response ceiling, and the tuple plus support
+citations are the whole remaining per-item cost. The amendment lets a field
+whose value is identical for every claim under one enclosing scope be stated
+once on that scope, under one inheritance rule stated in PWB-REQ-007: a claim
+carries the nearest enclosing scope's value for any field it does not carry
+itself, and a claim whose value differs carries the field itself. Claim
+identity is never inherited. The machine answer never inherits and keeps
+every field on every claim. Every oracle expands scopes with its own
+statement of the rule, so the comparator still imports no rendering code and
+PWB-REQ-020's collapsed falsifier still fires when a scope value would hide a
+differing member. A render that would carry two distinct evaluation
+identities fails instead of hoisting either. Rejected: an inheritance rule
+known only to the renderer, and dropping tuple fields a reader is presumed
+not to need.
+
